# The Nature-Culture Distinction and the Future of Environmental Education.

**Authors:** Colwell, Thomas

## Abstract
Addresses the nature-culture distinction and argues that nature and culture are no longer helpful conceptual tools for acquiring an ecological understanding of the world. Discusses the subject matter of environmental education and the ambiguity of nature, earth systems education, human and nonhuman environments, urban and wilderness education, and science and the humanities. (JRH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ548128

